course: dictionary
lesson: 2388
title: One word, many shapes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Curl can be an action (a verb) or a thing (a noun). «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter» means the hedgehog bent its body into a tight round ball to rest. Here curl is an action.
explain: Curl can also name a shape: a curl of hair, or any spiral shape. «The Milky Way is a barred spiral galaxy, with spiral arms curling out from its centre» uses curling for a spiral shape. The clue is the word spiral, which tells you the shape twists round in a circle.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «An elephant often curls its trunk round things to pick them up» makes sense if curl means bend into a round shape. If you swap in a different meaning, like "shout", the sentence stops making sense.
fact: Curl means to bend into a round or spiral shape.
fact: A curl is a piece of hair that grows or is shaped in a round twist, or any spiral shape.
fact: «Curl up» means to lie with your arms and legs pulled close to your body.
fact: In the sentence about the tardigrade, it curls into a dry little barrel called a «tun», and it can wake up and walk off again when water is added.
fact: The same word can be a verb (to curl) and a noun (a curl), so check how it is used in the sentence.
exercise: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter.» What does curled up mean here? | Ran off quickly across the lawn | *Pulled its body into a tight round shape | Sang a happy song | Grew very tall and thin
exercise: «The Milky Way has spiral arms curling out from its centre.» What does curling mean here? | *Bending out in a spiral shape | Breaking into small pieces | Shining very brightly | Stretching out in a straight line
exercise: «An elephant often curls its trunk round things to pick them up.» What does curls mean in this sentence? | Hides its trunk under the grass | Shakes its trunk hard from side to side | *Bends its trunk round into a loop | Lifts its trunk straight up in the air
test: The word curl can be an action or a thing. In «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves», what kind of word is curled? | Adjective | Adverb | Noun | *Verb
test: «When its moss dries out, a tardigrade curls into a dry little barrel.» What does this tell you about the tardigrade's body? | It flies off into the sky | It turns into water | *It bends into a small, round shape | It stays long and stretched out
exam: Which meaning of curl is correct for «a curl of hair»? | *A piece of hair in a round twist | A kind of ice on a frozen pond | A bird's loud song | To sleep in a warm bed
